From fcb627f310ba5ef761848b71c6520d785b4e8b54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel-rg35xx <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:16:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] owl hdmi: EDID mode check by CEA code, per-mode aspect,
 quieter log

Matches the running RG35XX kernel:
- hdmi_check_vid_available() looks the mode's CEA code up in the EDID
  video format bitmap (the public source shifted it by the OWL_TV_MOD_*
  enum, so the EDID check tested unrelated bits);
- the boot HDMI mode is kept only when the sink supports it; the chosen
  mode is logged ("best_vid is %d"); best_vid now defaults to DVI instead
  of being left uninitialised when the EDID lists no known mode;
- hdmi_cm gains the AVI picture aspect (4:3 for 480p/576p, 16:9 for the
  HD modes and DVI), set with the mode and sent in the AVI infoframe
  (was always 16:9);
- no default_resolution property means no user mode (the public source
  passed a NULL name to strcmp);
- OWL_HDMI info printks off (errors stay).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
